S367 kake line 157 sec=## Registry cells= ['S367', 'Yahoo!検索 インフォセンター — リンク先のウェブページの巡回制限（ウェブページ内やサーバーでの設定） — https://info-search.yahoo.co.jp/archives/002852.php', 'docs', 'A', "**The operator's own rule for refusing the crawl of a page's link targets from the page or the server** — the meta tag and the server header, beside the per-link attribute S374 holds, and what each does to the page's own indexing", '§ リンク先のウェブページの巡回制限 ― ウェブページ内やサーバーでの設定 → メタタグを使用する方法 / サーバーで設定する方法 (更新日 2010年11月24日)', 'a page can refuse the crawl of the links it contains without refusing itself: the meta tag `index,nofollow` refuses the link targets and keeps the page indexable, `noindex,nofollow` refuses both, and the server-side equivalent is the `X-Robots-Tag: NOFOLLOW` header', 'mined', '2026-10-25', '180d', 'corpus/knowledge/yahoo-japan-rel-nofollow-semantics.md, corpus/knowledge/yahoo-japan-link-target-crawl-restriction.md']
S367 kotodama line 396 sec=## Registry cells= ['S367', 'Batsîkama, Patrício, and Álvaro Campelo. 2011. "A Catedral de São Salvador de Angola: história e memória de um lugar mítico." *Sæculum — Revista de História* 25: 161-179. João Pessoa: Universidade Federal da Paraíba. ISSN 0104-892X; no DOI printed. — https://periodicos.ufpb.br/index.php/srh/article/view/13999/7921 (direct plain request, HTTP 200, application/pdf, 313,891 bytes, 19 pages, read 2026-10-22; no challenge.)', 'paper', 'B', "the 1885 redrawing of Kongo society across the Portuguese colony, the Belgian Congo and the French colony; the two aims of the 1913-14 insurrection. Not the abolition, not the conference, not the kingship's ritual content. (tier note: B — peer-reviewed history article, but about the cathedral's memory; the 1885 colonial division and the 1913-14 insurrection are stated in passing.)", 'p. 174: "Com a colonização de Angola – oficialmente desde 1885 – desenha-se outro mapa da sociedade kôngo"; p. 174: "uma parte que reclama ser fundadora desse Mbânza Kôngo vive no Congo belga e outra na colônia francesa"; p. 173: "Entre 1913-1914, o católico Álvaro Mbûta lidera a insurreição"; p. 173: "destituir Dom Manuel Kiditu do trono Kôngo"', 'After 1885 the Kongo capital lay in Portuguese Angola while part of its founding population lived in the Belgian and French colonies, and the 1913-14 rising sought to depose Kiditu.', 'queued', '2026-10-22', '365d', '—']
S372 kake line 158 sec=## Registry cells= ['S372', 'Yahoo!検索 インフォセンター — サイト単位、ディレクトリ単位での巡回の拒否設定 1 — https://info-search.yahoo.co.jp/archives/002849.php', 'docs', 'A', '**The rules for the refusal file a publisher writes, as this operator states them** — where it goes, what its absence means, how a path name inside it is read, and what a site that cannot place a file at its root is to do instead', 'page body from 更新日 to § 大文字と小文字の区別 (更新日 2010年11月24日)', 'the file belongs at the site root, and a site with no file is treated as unrestricted; the crawler checks for the file on every crawl, so a newly placed file is followed on the next crawl while the index takes time to reflect it; the path names after the refusal and the allowance directives are case-sensitive, so three spellings name three directories; and a site that cannot place a file at its root cannot refuse the crawl with it and is told to refuse indexing with the meta tag instead', 'mined', '2026-10-25', '180d', 'corpus/knowledge/yahoo-japan-rel-nofollow-semantics.md, corpus/knowledge/yahoo-japan-robots-txt-refusal-rules.md']
S372 kotodama line 401 sec=## Registry cells= ['S372', 'Museu da Sociedade de Geografia de Lisboa, object record "Padrão de Santo Agostinho" (no inventory number shown on the page), Lisbon, viewed 2026-10-22. — https://museu.socgeografialisboa.pt/objectos/padrao-de-santo-agostinho/ (direct plain request, HTTP 200, text/html, 197,712 bytes. Access date 2026-10-22.)', 'docs', 'A', "the surviving Diogo Cão pillar from Cabo de Santa Maria: lioz stone, dated 1482-1483, pillar height 216 cm, column 169 cm, head 46x33x33 cm, column diameter 73 cm, about 300 kg; raised to mark the Portuguese arrival on that stretch of coast, replaced at the site by another commemorative mark in 1892 and the original brought to Lisbon. (tier note: A — the holding museum's own catalogue record for the object it curates; authoritative for this piece's identity, material, date band, size and provenance history. It is not a source for the voyages' chronology and says nothing about the Congo mouth.)", 'object data, date field: "1482-1483"; object data, material field: "Pedra (lios)"; description, first sentence: "Marco comemorativo erguido por Diogo Cão no Cabo de Santa Maria"; description, second sentence: "Em 1892 foi substituído por um outro marco comemorativo e o original trazido para Lisboa"', 'The Lisbon Geographical Society holds a 1482-1483 lioz pillar raised by Diogo Cão at Cabo de Santa Maria, replaced on site in 1892 and brought to Lisbon.', 'mined', '2026-10-22', '365d', 'corpus/knowledge/civilizations/kongo-kingdom.md']
S373 kake line 159 sec=## Registry cells= ['S373', 'Yahoo!検索 インフォセンター — サイト単位、ディレクトリ単位での巡回の拒否設定 2 — https://info-search.yahoo.co.jp/archives/002850.php', 'docs', 'A', "**The operator's extended pattern syntax** — the two pattern symbols and the prefix-versus-end rule that decides whether a path rule matches more than its author intended", '§「*」記号 → 注意 and §「$」記号 → 注意 (更新日 2010年11月24日)', 'the wildcard matches any run of characters anywhere in the URL and the end marker matches only at the end; without the end marker the crawler treats the written string as a prefix and every URL containing it matches, so a rule meant for one file class can refuse a whole class of pages; and two refusal lines differing only by a trailing wildcard are equivalent', 'mined', '2026-10-25', '180d', 'corpus/knowledge/yahoo-japan-rel-nofollow-semantics.md, corpus/knowledge/baidu-friendly-crawl-guidance.md, corpus/knowledge/yahoo-japan-robots-pattern-syntax.md']
S373 kotodama line 402 sec=## Registry cells= ['S373', 'Lacerda, Teresa. "Rocks Ielala". *Encyclopaedia of Portuguese Expansion* (EVE), CHAM – NOVA FCSH / Universidade dos Açores, 2009; English translation by Maria das Mercês Pacheco. — https://eve.fcsh.unl.pt/en/places/rocks-ielala (direct plain request, HTTP 200, text/html, 21,526 bytes. Access date 2026-10-22.)', 'docs', 'B', "where the Ielala rocks are, that the carvings are attributed to the crew of Diogo Cão's second fleet, and the page's English rendering of the three rocks' texts (king, captain and companion on the first; two names on the second; four names on the third). (tier note: B — a named scholar's summary entry in a university reference work, with a named translator; it reports the rocks and their reading but is not the epigraphic edition, gives no letter-by-letter transcription, and cites no inscription corpus.)", 'opening description: "Ielala rocks, situated on the left bank of the Zaire River, close to the Ielala Falls, approximately 150 km from the river\'s mouth"; second sentence: "inscriptions made by the crew of the second fleet captained by Diogo Cão"; first-rock passage: "Here came the ships of the enlightened King João II of Portugal Diogo Cão Pêro da Costa"; second-rock passage: "Álvaro Pires and Pêro Escobar"', 'The Ielala rocks about 150 km up the Zaire carry second-fleet inscriptions naming João II, Diogo Cão and Pêro da Costa, plus crew names.', 'mined', '2026-10-22', '365d', 'corpus/knowledge/civilizations/kongo-kingdom.md']
S390 kake line 160 sec=## Registry cells= ['S390', '百度搜索资源平台 — 百度Spider新增渲染抓取UA公告 — https://ziyuan.baidu.com/wiki/990', 'docs', 'A', "**Whether Baidu's own crawler fetches a page's CSS, JavaScript and images** — the platform's own announcement of a dedicated render user agent", '§ announcement body, the paragraph above 最新UA如下 and the two agent strings under it (发布日期 2017-03-24, printed on the page)', "Baidu states it needs to fetch a site's CSS, JavaScript and images to understand and index the page, and from 2017-03-24 it fetches them with a dedicated agent `Baiduspider-render/2.0`, which it asks publishers not to block; the announcement says the crawler fetches those resources and does not say it executes the script", 'mined', '2026-10-25', '180d', 'corpus/knowledge/baidu-friendly-crawl-guidance.md, corpus/knowledge/baidu-mobile-matching-error-causes.md']
S390 kotodama line 419 sec=## Registry cells= ['S390', 'Bostoen, Koen, Odjas Ndonda Tshiyayi, and Gilles-Maurice de Schryver. 2013. "On the origin of the royal Kongo title ngangula." *Africana Linguistica* 19: 53-83. Open repository copy, University of Pretoria (UPSpace). — https://repository.up.ac.za/bitstreams/902842e3-d5eb-4688-bf3f-40b310b24959/download (direct plain request (curl), HTTP 200, `application/pdf`, 2,360,681 bytes, 31 pages, read with `pdftotext -layout`; no challenge, paywall or login met, 2026-10-22.)', 'paper', 'A', "what the royal titles `ngangula`, `ntinu` and `ntotila` are and that they co-exist; the literal sense of `ngangula a Kongo`; the `Mwene Vunda` office in the selection and coronation of kings; the kinship-titled lordship of Mbata and the naming chain of the founder's line (`Nsaku Lau`, `Nimi a Nzima`, `Lukeni lua Nimi` also called `Ntinu Wene`); a royal style that carries a Christian name (`Pedro II Afonso`). Not a source for the `mani` form, the number of provinces, regalia inventories, minkisi, or royal chronology. (tier note: A — a peer-reviewed historical-linguistic study whose subject is exactly this: the etymology and title status of `ngangula` and the other royal Kongo titles. Tier B for the political history it reports from Thornton and Vansina, which the entry should cite through those authors if it leans on it.)", 'p. 55, Introduction: "ngangula a Kongo literally means ‘blacksmith of Kongo’"; p. 55, Introduction: "which co-exists with others such as ntinu and ntotila"; p. 69, on Alvaro II\'s burial and Pedro II\'s coronation: "the Mwene Vunda (an official who played an important role in the selection and coronation of the kings)"; p. 73, on Mbata and the founder traditions: "father of the bride of Nimi a Nzima, himself father of Lukeni lua Nimi or Ntinu Wene"', 'Kongo royal style stacked Kikongo titles — ngangula, literally "blacksmith of Kongo", ntinu and ntotila — while selection and coronation belonged partly to the Mwene Vunda office.', 'mined', '2026-10-22', '365d', 'corpus/knowledge/civilizations/kongo-kingdom.md']
S409 kake line 161 sec=## Registry cells= ['S409', '百度搜索资源平台 — 百度Spider渲染UA在移动端全流量上线 — https://ziyuan.baidu.com/wiki/1021', 'docs', 'A', '**What the operator says about its render user agent once it carries real traffic** — the crawl-path side of the rendering question', "§ the article body's beta-and-rollout passage (发布日期 2017-06-07)", 'the operator says it introduced the render user agent in March 2017, beta-tested it on mobile and PC, and that during the beta the crawl-volume anomalies it analysed were not caused by the render agent; the agent is now on full mobile traffic and not yet on all PC traffic; the page does not say the agent executes script', 'mined', '2026-10-25', '180d', 'corpus/knowledge/baidu-friendly-crawl-guidance.md, corpus/knowledge/baidu-mobile-matching-error-causes.md']
S409 kotodama line 438 sec=## Registry cells= ['S409', 'Thornton, Dora. 2015. *Made of Straw of Rare Beauty: Kongo Textiles in Renaissance European Collections*. Exhibition blog post, *Kongo: Power and Majesty*, The Metropolitan Museum of Art, posted 2 October 2015; author is Curator of Renaissance Europe and the Waddesdon Bequest, British Museum. No DOI; stable URL as captured. — https://web.archive.org/web/20151110063110/http://www.metmuseum.org/exhibitions/listings/2015/kongo/blog/posts/kongo-textiles-renaissance-european-collections (live URL answered HTTP 429 on two plain requests (rate-limit response page, 34223 bytes) — a throttle, not a challenge or a login; the post was read from Wayback capture `20151110063110` of the same URL (mobile rendering, same text), HTTP 200, 34702 bytes, 2026-10-22)', 'docs', 'B', "the finishing technique described by a missionary; the comparison Europeans made with Italian silk velvet and the Pacheco Pereira judgement; the geometric pattern language and the curator's reading of it as meaningful rather than decorative; the European afterlife of these cloths in Kunstkammern from Prague in 1607 and in Sweden and Denmark; the Settala and Kircher annotations, including the Kircher description that puts the cloth in the Kingdom of Angola; one dated object caption (Pitt Rivers 1886.1.254.1, 17th–18th century, inventoried 1883). It carries **no** Kongo-side evidence: no maker, no price, no grade, no owner. (tier note: B — a museum-published exhibition essay by a curator of the field, quotable for object identifications, for the collection history it reports and for the early-modern quotations it reproduces; it is an essay with no apparatus, its early-modern quotations are second-hand (it gives no page for Zuchelli or Pacheco Pereira), and it is not the exhibition catalogue. A only for the Pitt Rivers caption data it prints.)", 'Body paragraph 2, on Zuchelli (1663–1716), Italian missionary to the Kongo, as the essay quotes him: "with a knife they cut the cloth in the proper spots and rub it well with their hands, so that it looks like patterned velvet"; Body paragraph 2, as the essay quotes Duarte Pacheco Pereira (ca. 1460–1533): "that those made in Italy do not surpass them in workmanship"; Body paragraph 3, on the design: "Bands of sophisticated geometric patterns spiral across the textile surfaces"; Body paragraph 7, a description of 1709 quoted in the essay: "four mats made with admirable skill in the Kingdom of Angola"', "A British Museum curator's Met exhibition essay describes Kongo raffia velvet finished by cutting and rubbing, and records such cloths in European Kunstkammern from Prague in 1607.", 'mined', '2026-10-22', '365d', 'corpus/knowledge/civilizations/kongo-kingdom.md']
